   <text type="letter">
      
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline>LAWRENCE HALL, KIRKLAND STREET<lb/>
                  <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__82" type="place">CAMBRIDGE, MASSACHUSETTS
                     </rs><lb/><date when="1943-08-02">August 2, 1943</date></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Paul</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I hope you don&apos;t mind my bothering you with this letter but I wanted you to know
               that I fully understand that you may consider its content with divided feelings. You
               may think that the action as a whole may not have great practical effect and,
               secondly, that it may endanger the people who are on the list. We have discussed
               these questions many times in our committee meetings, not only within the smaller
               committee itself but also with scholars from abroad on whose judgment we lay value.
               They all agree that the step proposed in this letter is necessary and it is now
               almost impossible to add more caution to the procedure than has been provided. So
               please devote an hour to this letter and give me your reaction as soon as possible.
               This letter has been sent to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1209" type="person"
                  >Professor Löwe</rs>, <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1099" type="person">Professor
                  Kroner</rs>, <rs ref="#" type="person">Professor
                  Salomon</rs><!-- unklar wer gemeint ist, vielleicht Gottfried Salomon oder Albert Salomon -->,<rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__846" type="person">Professor Heimann</rs>, and <rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__2095" type="person">Mr. Kurt Wolff</rs>.</p><closer>
            <salute>Cordially yours,</salute>
            <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1965" type="person"
            ><hi rend="hand">Robert Ulich</hi><lb/>Robert Ulich</rs></signed>
            <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Paul Tillich</rs><lb/>
               99 Claremont Avenue<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York, New York</rs><lb/>
               u.s
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
